# Group-Chat Pod Manifest — <Pod Name>

A pod is a group chat in Hermes Desktop Bot Mode that organizes a sub-division of the team
around an area of focus. Rooms deliberate; the board records commitments.

## Purpose
One sentence: what this pod exists to decide and produce.

## Area of focus
- <research / product-build / content / operations / ...>

## Members (2–6)
| Bot | Role | Why in this pod |
|-----|------|-----------------|
| <bot name> | <role> | <contribution> |
| <bot name> | <role> | <contribution> |

If more than 6 Bots want in, split the pod. A room >6 gets noisy; the hard cap protects it.

## Standing agenda
- What the pod reviews weekly / at milestone.
- What the pod escalates to the human (`@user`).

## Coordination rules
- Use the board for commitments; use the room for deliberation.
- @-mention to target one member; mention nobody to get the round.
- A pod decision that needs to persist becomes a kanban card. (Reference the card ID in
  the room.)

## Creation
1. Hermes Desktop → Bots tab → New Group Chat → name it `<Pod Name>`.
2. Add the members above (local Bots, or from registered Connections for cross-machine).
3. Pin a link to this manifest in a message so members can cite it.

---

**Maintainer note:** create one manifest per pod under your team's docs (or in the vault).
Keep it short — the pod's job is deciding, not maintaining paperwork.
